us\/exit\/source\/integrity\/cleanup evidence and the support boundary ARM64\/amd64 emulation. Owner summaries and author claims are not independent proof.\nAct as unfamiliar service engineer following the guide. Your priority is whether an unfamiliar engineer can obtain whole-table counts for huge service DBs without degradation, with explicit safe deferral where prerequisites cannot be met. Do not substitute engine encyclopedia or exhaustive grids. Challenge metadata visibility\/partition\/index doublecount, approximate vs exact vs stats-at-update, RLS count scope, bigint overflow, zero\/NULL\/permissions\/errors not empty, ROWVERSION read assumptions vs default locking RC, Sch-S\/DDL, tempdb\/PVS\/version retention, backup provisioning\/resource isolation\/shared readable secondaries\/redo\/freshness, commandtimeout vs locktimeout, query\/session ownership\/currentSPID\/cancellation\/serverend\/recovery, live workload conservation\/unfinished\/censored\/sparse windows, cache\/index\/order\/TDE state, client key vs server keys and unmeasured AlwaysEncrypted. Check claimed max\/min error and conditions by recomputing cited raw JSON; do not accept universal few%\/10% guarantees or N-only safe primary scan thresholds. No oldMySQL nonlocking assumptions imported. NOLOCK\/READPAST\/whole-table-lock or deliberate contention injection not allowed. Do not request excluded dangerous experiments. Counts must be RCSI or SNAPSHOT qualified; no automatic production isolationconfiguration change. Existing inventory\/approvedexport first, no primaryextraSQL withoutbudget, resourcecaps before monitoring, no viablepath=>defer. Compare simpler\/faster viable alternatives forrequiredprecision andfreshness, no unsupported globalranking. 100M\/80\/100col\/encryption actual measurement vs missing combinations must be distinguishable, nativeproductionperformance not inferred fromemulation.\nRaise only actual operational material defects with concrete scenario\/source\/evidence\/correction, not stylistic preferences. High\/middle and necessary measurement gaps block acceptance. Do not demand every possible experiment if safe explicitly limited guidance resolves the decision. Accept only exact current guide and linked details\/proof\/source verified, no blocking defect\/necessary experiment pending. Preserve failures\/unknowns, never mark skipped coveragepassed. Return SMALL JSON: accepted boolean, decision accepted\/rejected, role, guidelineSha256, proofSha256, findings array(id,severity,scenario,evidence,requiredCorrection), requestedExperiments array(onlyindispensable,whydecisiondepends), reviewQuestions object(betterMethods,designCoverage,omissions,lockFactors,fastCount), reviewEvidence array concrete files\/fields\/hash\/recomputation. Do not assert otherrole acceptance without artifact.\n\nRead results\/sqlserver\/reviews\/owner-open-findings.json and independently verify the actual corrections to every owner material finding; disposition labels alone are not proof.\n\nExact inputs: {\"guideSha256\": \"a2430a338a44b52103009c9612020898c2066c0d18836a39532067f77f3e95bb\", \"proofSha256\": \"83067594c7760061f4c74145b11916ee2f70b8f7343086e7abe49e93e2e26d11\"}","mergedVariables":{"_rielaInput":{"communicationIds":[],"messages":[],"sourceStepIds":[],"stepId":"review","workflowExecutionId":"temp-sqlserver-count-engineer-sol-session-38"},"availableMemories":{"node":[],"workflow":[]},"memoryCommandHelp":"","nodeId":"review","nodeKind":"worker","runtimeVariables":{"_rielaInput":{"communicationIds":[],"messages":[],"sourceStepIds":[],"stepId":"review","workflowExecutionId":"temp-sqlserver-count-engineer-sol-session-38"}},"workflowDescription":"Separate Sol adversarial SQL Server count review engineer","workflowId":"temp-sqlserver-count-engineer-sol"},"promptText":"You are a separate new GPT-6.1 Sol adversarial reviewer of the SQL Server whole-table count guideline. READ ONLY: no writing, DB\/Docker connections, measurements, delegation, workflows, commit 